 "last_change": "Corpus grew, not a regression. MASTER_CROSSWALK.tsv joined the scan as an EXISTENCE_ONLY source on 2026-09-07, adding 999 distinct ChEBI ids: 17 do not resolve (NOT_FOUND) and 5 are obsolete. Label diffing is deliberately NOT applied to it - measured 25.9% mismatch that is VMH naming convention vs ChEBI's (Pyruvate/pyruvic acid), which is the false-positive rate that kills a gate. Also fixed here: OLS4 answers 400, not 404, from /properties for a non-property IRI, so every genuinely nonexistent id was returning _error and counted as 'could not look it up' rather than NOT_FOUND. That gap is where the 17 dead ids were hiding. Separately, 2 of the prior 22 (FOODON:03411347, NCBITaxon:1126) no longer appear anywhere in the tree - fixed by other work since 2026-08-29 without the baseline being lowered. Prior WRONG_CONCEPT debt is therefore 20, not 22.",
